course: dictionary
lesson: 14087
title: Quiet and gentle: the word meekly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Meekly» is an adverb. An adverb tells us how something is done. «Meekly» means in a quiet, gentle way, without arguing or fighting back. Think of a child who is told to tidy up and simply nods and does it, with no fuss.
explain: «She took the medicine meekly, without a word.» The word «meekly» tells you how she took it: quietly, and without refusing. Look for clues in the words around it, such as «without a word» or «without arguing».
explain: «Meekly» does not always mean good or bad. Sometimes it shows gentleness and kindness. Other times it shows someone giving in too easily, when they could have stood up for themselves. The sentence around the word tells you which one it is.
fact: An adverb tells us how, when or where something happens. «Meekly» tells us how.
fact: «Meekly» means in a quiet, gentle way, without arguing or fighting back.
fact: «Meek» is the adjective: a meek person is quiet and gentle, and does not argue.
fact: In stories, «meekly» often shows a character giving in or obeying without a word, sometimes too easily.
fact: «Blessed are the meek» means blessed are people who are gentle and humble.
exercise: «The puppy followed its owner home meekly, with its tail down.» How did the puppy follow? | Angrily, pulling on the lead | Far behind, and lost | Very loudly, barking all the way | *Quietly and gently, without fuss
exercise: «Ben meekly handed over his toy when his sister asked.» What does meekly suggest? | Ben shouted and grabbed the toy back | *Ben gave in quietly, without arguing | Ben was not in the room | Ben hid the toy under the bed
exercise: Which word could replace «meekly» in «She meekly agreed to go to bed»? | Madly | *Without arguing | Angrily | Loudly
test: «The knight meekly gave up his sword when the king asked.» What does meekly mean here? | Happily, with a big smile | Proudly, with a loud shout | Quickly, to win a prize | *Quietly, without fighting back
test: «Alice sometimes answers meekly when the creatures are rude.» Does Alice fight back? | No, she answers with a loud laugh | *No, she answers quietly, without arguing | Yes, she runs away and hides | Yes, she shouts back at every creature
exam: Which sentence uses «meekly» correctly? | The loud band meekly played until midnight | The sky meekly roared with thunder | *The little boy meekly said sorry and took the blame | She meekly won the race by a mile
